      "id": "ccna-default-access-membership",
      "topic": "Default VLAN membership",
      "title": "Move a new desk out of default VLAN 1",
      "summary": "Put a new desk in its workgroup while preserving the working default-VLAN devices.",
      "explanation": "The desk uses its workgroup’s VLAN while the existing legacy devices still share VLAN 1. The trunk’s native setting stays in place.",
      "hints": [
        "The desk’s access setting and both trunk native settings have different roles.",
        "Find the Shipping Peer’s access VLAN in the station table.",
        "Test both the changed workgroup pair and the unchanged legacy pair."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://learningcontent.cisco.com/documents/marketing/exam-topics/200-301-CCNA-v1.1.pdf",
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/catalyst9300/software/release/17-1/configuration_guide/int_hw/b_171_int_and_hw_9300_cg/configuring_interface_characteristics.html"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Two fixed connected switches with deliberate static access or trunk mode, existing normal-range VLANs and mutual Ethernet broadcast checks. No IOS parser, DTP, VTP, voice policy, STP or real network.",
      "prerequisites": [
        "ccna-vlan-native"
      ],
      "objective": "Move the Shipping Desk into the same Ethernet segment as the Shipping Peer. Keep the two legacy devices working together, separate from the Shipping Desk.",
      "retry_guidance": "Read which part of the Ethernet or IPv4 path did not work, then test again.",
      "guide": [
        {
          "title": "Understand the task",
          "why": "A default access choice still assigns the port to VLAN 1 in this switch model. Clearing an explicit choice returns it to that default. A station normally sends its access port an untagged Ethernet frame.",
          "action": "Verify the supplied path.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Try the separate example",
          "why": "The native VLAN tells a trunk how to carry untagged frames between switches. Both ends of the supplied trunk agree on VLAN 88. This setting has no effect on the desk’s default access VLAN.",
          "action": "Verify the supplied path.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Complete the independent assignment",
          "why": "An Ethernet connection may be up while a desk is in the wrong group. Use an Ethernet broadcast to see who can receive a frame. Check the legacy pair separately after making a change.",
          "action": "Verify the supplied path.",
          "commands": []
        }
      ],
